ool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54402, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QLUxufPLJAs1FYnWK8x41k", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54402, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QLUxufPLJAs1FYnWK8x41k", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 58195, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The latest release, v2.3.1, and its release candidate v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, so us-west and eu-west were briefly still on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n- **Incident:** The create request timed out, but the incident list shows it was created, so I didn't send it again and there's only one page. INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial first attempt) and two follow-ups:\n  - find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure\n  - look into the orchestrator error", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016qkFNUn7cf22BXcM39kRf7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GCRWrS44ztkMkU7Amxggcf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "t