ng rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01QLUxufPLJAs1FYnWK8x41k", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The latest release, v2.3.1, and its release candidate v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, so us-west and eu-west were briefly still on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n- **Incident:** The create request timed out, but the incident list shows it was created, so I didn't send it again and there's only one page. INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial first attempt) and two follow-ups:\n  - find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure\n  - look into the orchestrator error", "type": "text"}]}]}